decisions:
  - id: gap-narration-doctor-only
    decision: Gap narration ships in paradigm doctor and postflight, NOT in the stop hook
    rationale: 'Jinx: stop hook value is terseness, verbosity kills compliance. Sage: adaptive verbosity is right long-term but overkill for v1. Sentinel: gap narrations are attack surface maps, must be Ring 1 project-locked, never relayed via Symphony.'
  - id: activity-metrics-not-dollars
    decision: Track tool call count, payload size, session duration per agent — NOT dollar costs
    rationale: 'Jinx: MCP tools cannot see token counts, dollar costs are guesses. Sage: showing costs creates behavioral distortion (developers avoid Opus when it''s the right choice). Revisit when Claude Code exposes token usage in hooks.'
  - id: soft-provenance-not-dag
    decision: Add optional parentId and lineageType fields to NotebookEntry, not a full DAG
    rationale: 'Jinx: migration destroys simplicity that makes notebooks adoptable. YAML stays human-readable. Architect''s full DAG is v2 design if soft provenance proves valuable. Sentinel: requires prepareForPublish() sanitization before any nevr.land integration.'
  - id: outcome-tracking-phase1-only
    decision: Instrument notebook reference recording in session work log, defer effective_rate scoring
    rationale: 'Jinx: Goodhart''s Law will destroy notebook quality — easy-to-follow entries score high, nuanced entries get pruned. Attribution problem unsolved. Collect data first, analyze after 50+ sessions.'
  - id: change-based-health-not-time
    decision: Track compliance trend (improving/stable/degrading) from stop hook violation frequency, not time-based staleness
    rationale: 'Jinx: time-based staleness creates false positives for stable code. Stop hook already does change-based freshness. Conductor health dot based on violation trends, not maxStaleDuration.'
  - id: tool-aliases-not-embeddings
    decision: Improve tool descriptions with aliases field instead of semantic embedding retrieval
    rationale: 'Jinx: domain vocabulary blindness means general embeddings won''t match paradigm_ripple to ''show dependencies''. Existing 3-tier system works offline, zero latency, no dependencies. Revisit at 200+ tools.'
  - id: security-prerequisites
    decision: '4 security items ship before or alongside P1: new ContentCategory entries, notebook-publish boundary, Symphony content filtering, NotebookEntry shareability field'
    rationale: 'Sentinel audit found: no notebook-publish enforcement boundary exists, Symphony relay has no content-type filtering, ContentCategory is incomplete for new data types. These are architectural prerequisites.'
  - id: university-restructuring-shipped
    decision: 'Shipped v5.31.0 with 8-phase university restructuring: PARA 001 Quick Start, enforcement/shift/quick-check/conductor lessons, quiz WHAT→HOW upgrades'
    rationale: Audit found courses teach WHAT (57%) more than HOW (43%), no day-1 course, First Steps buried at lesson 8/9. Now 8 courses, 82 lessons, 361 quizzes, HOW-first throughout new content.
learnings:
  - Jinx's stress-testing prevented 2 features from shipping with fundamental flaws (semantic retrieval domain blindness, time-based staleness false positives) and reshaped 4 others into simpler, more honest versions
  - 'Sage''s UX principle — ''Paradigm should feel like a competent coworker who keeps things organized in the background'' — resolved every visibility debate: invisible by default, on-demand for power users, never blocking unless enforcement level demands it'
  - Sentinel identified that gap narrations are attack surface maps and Symphony relay has no content-type filtering — both are architectural gaps that must be fixed before features that produce sensitive metadata
  - The cross-study pattern of quality-decay-curves appeared independently in AnyTool and ClawWork — this is an emerging standard pattern the industry is converging on
  - Architect's designs were architecturally sound but Jinx correctly identified that 3 of 6 features solve theoretical problems (semantic retrieval at 50 tools, time-based staleness, dollar cost tracking without data) rather than real ones
